      <room>AW1.121</room>
      <slug></slug>
      <title>Refactoring Stored Routines</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>MySQL</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Although MySQL stored routines have their drawbacks, especially performance-wise, they still have their use. However, there are many things that can go wrong, and in many cases, observing a few principles, and adopting a few coding habits can have huge benefits for performance and maintainability of your stored routines.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;  </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;In this presentation, I will present a few cases and perform a few stepwise improvements to refactor the stored routine. Benchmarks are presented to show how each change improves performance.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;  </description>
      <persons>
          <person id="2221">Roland Bouman</person>
      </persons>
      <links></links>
      <video></video>
      <end></end>
  </event>